# km-panic escape hatch (host-local, never commit a disabled gate)
gate.json.disabled

# Agent worktrees: nested git repos, host-local by construction. Left
# visible to `git add -A`, each one makes gate-check's dirtyTreeId() emit
# "warning: adding embedded git repository" — noise that flooded the 4096-
# byte block-reason tail and hid a real test failure (2026-08-08) — and
# folds worktree content into the tree hash, so an edit under a worktree
# reads as a repo change to tier-0 suite selection. Branches are unaffected:
# ignoring the checkout never touches the refs it points at.
.claude/worktrees/

# census probe: staged benchmark inputs (reconstruct from TB2 checkout; canary data, do not track)
